# Release maintenance

## Tools releases

Run `make release TAG=0.8.0` after the selected tag exists. `TAG` is mandatory
and must identify a Git tag, not a branch or commit hash. The command exports
that tag's committed tree into `build/freedict-tools-0.8.0.tar.xz`, with a
`tools/` directory inside. Use `BUILD_DIR=/path/to/output` to change the output
directory. Hierarchical tag names use hyphens in the archive filename.

HEAD may have newer commits; a warning is printed and the tagged tree is still
exported. Untracked files and uncommitted edits are excluded. Each invocation
regenerates the archive, replacing an existing file only after export succeeds.

## Remote access

All dictionaries, both from the fd-dictionaries repository and the generated
dictionaries need to be present for release operations.
Hence, `make api`, `make need-update`, and dictionary deployment acquire remote
access and clean up within one process. `fd_tool` manages this in the
background. Depending on the FreeDict configuration, it either uses SSHFS or
Unison for making files available.

`fd_file_mgr --run COMMAND [ARGS...]` exists to perform manual operations with all dictionaries available.
On a failure, `fd_file_mgr -m` and `fd_file_mgr -u` perform mounting and unmounting, respectively.
